From: MikolajQ <1713112+MikolajQ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:59:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] audio: battery_listener: don't join a thread twice and
 re-init after a health death

BatteryListenerImpl::init() starts the status thread only when a HIDL
health@2.0 service is found; upstream now checks mThread for null before
joining it (399ade9), which covers AIDL-only health HALs (rhode:
android.hardware.health-service.qti).

serviceDied() still joins the thread without waking it, so it can wait
forever, keeps the joined thread around, so the destructor joins it
again and std::thread throws, and keeps the stale mHealth, so init()
refuses to run again. Wake the thread, join it only if joinable, drop
the old handles, then re-init.
---
 hal/audio_extn/battery_listener.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hal/audio_extn/battery_listener.cpp b/hal/audio_extn/battery_listener.cpp
index 14be797..3a9ea75 100644
--- a/hal/audio_extn/battery_listener.cpp
+++ b/hal/audio_extn/battery_listener.cpp
@@ -169,7 +169,8 @@ BatteryListenerImpl::BatteryListenerImpl(cb_fn_t cb) :
 
 BatteryListenerImpl::~BatteryListenerImpl()
 {
-    if (mThread != NULL) {
+    // serviceDied() may have joined the thread already; joining twice throws.
+    if (mThread != NULL && mThread->joinable()) {
         mThread->join();
     }
 }
@@ -195,11 +196,14 @@ void BatteryListenerImpl::serviceDied(uint64_t cookie __unused,
         }
         ALOGI("health service died, reinit");
         mDone = true;
+        mCond.notify_one();
     }
-    if (mThread != NULL) {
+    if (mThread != NULL && mThread->joinable()) {
         mThread->join();
     }
+    mThread.reset();
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> _l(mLock);
+    mHealth = nullptr;
     init();
 }
 
